{"case":{"approved_prefix":"requests/","command":["python","/verification/verify.py"],"entry_files":["requests/sessions.py"],"entry_lines":{"requests/sessions.py":44},"id":"psf__requests-1921","image":"sha256:9f1fdb06b595456c36483ed2c7a008c33be33e311fdb257c1bb29db812b00a85","issue":"Removing a default header of a session\n[The docs](http://docs.python-requests.org/en/latest/user/advanced/#session-objects) say that you can prevent sending a session header by setting the headers value to None in the method's arguments. You would expect (as [discussed on IRC](https://botbot.me/freenode/python-requests/msg/10788170/)) that this would work for session's default headers, too:\n\n``` python\nsession = requests.Session()\n# Do not send Accept-Encoding\nsession.headers['Accept-Encoding'] = None\n```\n\nWhat happens is that \"None\"  gets sent as the value of header.\n\n```\nAccept-Encoding: None\n```\n\nFor the reference, here is a way that works:\n\n``` python\ndel session.headers['Accept-Encoding']\n```\n\n","issue_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/1921","provenance":"Build004 curated SWE-bench Verified case; human-localized entry files. Public training contamination possible. Entry files and line windows derive from historical maintainer localization; reference text is not supplied to the model.","qualified":true,"reference_digest":"33fc461de67706a7d3c91008799489d6d1e6b521bfc0131dd22c4959d00b9f08","repository":"psf/requests","revision":"3c88e520da24ae6f736929a750876e7654accc3d","source_digest":"90d3195657bb2ef5687535738f18ebe71b3b46f41ec572493f59604e74562303","source_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/tree/3c88e520da24ae6f736929a750876e7654accc3d","split":"evaluation","title":"Removing a default header of a session","verification_digest":"d00ea64ccaa3241b1bf2757e09de87d6c4cc73ca6ec31a87e28b8fa200209d05"},"registry_version":"repository-cases-v1"}